{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/476538-bale-hounds-how-powerfull-are-maeltinet","id":476538,"title":"[Bale Hounds] How powerfull are Maeltinet?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-10T20:18:57-07:00","id":476538,"title":"[Bale Hounds] How powerfull are Maeltinet?","content":"Question is in the title, but I'm mostly asking about relative Rank of those corrupted spirits. But I would not despised other possible powers of them.<br /> <br /> I ask, as I run chronicle based on fight with Bale Hounds pack, placed in Sweden. Idea is that those Hounds are rather powerful, old pack that rules small town. They do not have one Totem, but are rather alliance of Hounds for various Maeljinns ( Seven Deadly Sins ), with each werewolf represent one. Each one of them have it's own, personal Totem - and I think that various Maeltinet would be suitable for this role.<br /> <br /> What Rank and powers could those spirits have and grant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T20:56:19-07:00","id":476579,"title":"","content":"The Maeltinet are detailed mostly in Lore of the Forsaken and Blasphemies, but range from rank 3 to 4. They are avatars and aspects and servants of the Maeljin, so most often the totems for Bale Hounds that aren't hiding among 'regular' packs. Lore of the Forsaken has a number of write-ups for them, I believe one for each Maeljin, all rank 4. In the Blasphemies book, on page 131, the rules for Maeltinet Totem Creation can be found, but I'd suggest throwing in some odd gifts and abilities from Inferno that suit the spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-11-2015, 12:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T22:13:07-07:00","id":476634,"title":"","content":"Can't a truly &quot;badass&quot; Bale Hound be reborn as a Maeltinet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T22:38:15-07:00","id":476671,"title":"","content":"That's the belief, yes. They're called the Maeladar. Obviously it's up to the storyteller to decide whether it's valid or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T00:21:06-07:00","id":476737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/476538-bale-hounds-how-powerfull-are-maeltinet?p=476579#post476579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Maeltinet are detailed mostly in Lore of the Forsaken and Blasphemies, but range from rank 3 to 4. They are avatars and aspects and servants of the Maeljin, so most often the totems for Bale Hounds that aren't hiding among 'regular' packs. Lore of the Forsaken has a number of write-ups for them, I believe one for each Maeljin, all rank 4. In the Blasphemies book, on page 131, the rules for Maeltinet Totem Creation can be found, but I'd suggest throwing in some odd gifts and abilities from Inferno that suit the spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>As how much they are &quot;avatars&quot; of Maeljins and how much general spirits of Sins? I proper one Maeltinet for each Hound, and for now I have an &quot;angelic&quot; spirit of monotheistic religion xenophobia ( Influences Envy 4, Faith 3 ) and spiderous spirit of greed and favors, like &quot;web of connections&quot; ( Influences Greed 4, Spiders 3 ). Or are Maeltinets more wolf like? Or more &quot;demonic&quot; in general sense, like random storms of ephemera?<br /> <br /> I would also hear, if you got, ideas for Maeltinets connected with Seven Deadly Sins, especially for Wrath ( or Rage in WtF setting ). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T09:48:03-07:00","id":477057,"title":"","content":"They seem to be much more avatars than general spirits. They're the Lords of Wounds, and Wound-spirits aren't considered normal spirits anymore, they're infected by the Maeljin of the Inferno. They may have started out as spirits, but they were corrupted by a Maeljin or a Maeljin's tainted wound. They may have started off as a Maeljin's demonic whispers, urging a spirit to corruption until it gave in, or it may have started off as a Bale Hound that served the Maeljin spectacularly with the Maeltinet urging it along with dark prophesies. With the new system, it's unclear if there are still 'just' 9 Maeljin, so you're free to start a foundation for them however you want.<br /> <br /> For specifics, you could probably built it around the area. A Wrath spirit might be a spirit of hate crimes, which seem to be on the rise there, in fact the totem of the Eiwaz Mot is theorized by some to be a Maeltinet, but of Violence. I don't know much about the history of Sweden. There was a movie, Wither, also called Vittra, that had some sort of hateful spirit spreading a zombie plague in the woods in the area. There's the history of the Vikings. If you want something more recent you might just go with something more personal. A wound forming when one person, angry at another or others, inspired people to do something horrible about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T10:34:51-07:00","id":477075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/476538-bale-hounds-how-powerfull-are-maeltinet?p=477057#post477057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For specifics, you could probably built it around the area. A Wrath spirit might be a spirit of hate crimes, which seem to be on the rise there, in fact the totem of the Eiwaz Mot is theorized by some to be a Maeltinet, but of Violence. I don't know much about the history of Sweden. There was a movie, Wither, also called Vittra, that had some sort of hateful spirit spreading a zombie plague in the woods in the area. There's the history of the Vikings. If you want something more recent you might just go with something more personal. A wound forming when one person, angry at another or others, inspired people to do something horrible about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hate crimes are out of question, as setting is small settelment on the edge of Lapland. But you mentioned Vikings, and even if most sources point that they do not dwell so much on North in those times, I have in-game fact of this settlement being build by the Viking Uratha leader that lead his clan up to those mountains, where they fight with local Ursara and native Sami people. In the end, the humans mingeled, but the Ursara were cast out of they land, and become slowly daying breed in local. I was thinking about using somewhere this fact, so maybe do a Maeltinet that was once a Firstborn brood once ( Winter Wolf or Fenris Destroyer ) that was Totem of this leader Uratha and by astrocieties of this conflict, it become Wound spirit?<br /> <br /> Then is also think I want to do - the NPC that will be this Rage Maeltinet Hound, will be once PCs pack member. She will return to them, to inflirtrate and break the group. But the Totem of the pack, Light of Dead, is Bear Spirit of Death that was largly connected with Ursara before and was one of the larger forces fighting with Viking ansectors of now pack. Would not this kind of spirit sence that NPC Hound is bound with his ancient enemy? Will he sense his enemies in nearby, where the Maeltinet would be summoned?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T10:57:01-07:00","id":477087,"title":"","content":"Go read Lore of the Forsaken for some pretty nasty examples of maeltinents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T17:38:44-07:00","id":477394,"title":"","content":"The good type of nasty. Pages 57-58 would probably be of particular interest to Wyrdhamster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T02:44:42-07:00","id":477728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/476538-bale-hounds-how-powerfull-are-maeltinet?p=477394#post477394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The good type of nasty. Pages 57-58 would probably be of particular interest to Wyrdhamster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I read about Dreadwolf and I like his concept very much. But does he not strong enought for his Rank 4? Influances only in Anger 2 and Murder 2, where he could have something like Anger 4, Murder 3, Wolf 2, for example? I do not know, don't the Maeltinents should be <i>avatars</i> of Maeljins, not only random servants?<br /> <br /> I want to use those Totems in 2ED game - does not they should be more powerfull in Influances? What Bane would be suitable for Dreadwolf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T03:02:22-07:00","id":477731,"title":"","content":"An avatar is not an exact replica of something, it represents an aspect working towards the goals of the progenitor. Start mixing Infernal demons with Hisil Spirit symbolism and you get something that doesn't look physically like its progenitor. Also, just because something is Rank 4 doesn't mean it will have maxed out stats and influences, if you feel it isn't challenging enough for your players you have room to make tweaks, if you start out maxed out you don't have much room to work with (plus those were some early examples of Spirits, mechanics have changed).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T03:27:04-07:00","id":477762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/476538-bale-hounds-how-powerfull-are-maeltinet?p=477731#post477731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(plus those were some early examples of Spirits, mechanics have changed).</div> </div> </div> </div>Understand your previous points, but this is interesting - are there guidlines of how many or how much powerfull Influnaces should have spirits on each Rank, roughly? Like &quot;One Influance on Rank level, and each other one level lower than previous one&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T03:46:48-07:00","id":477772,"title":"","content":"The rules for Influences are clearly stated in the corebook.<br /> <br /> A spirit gets Influence dots equal to their Rank, which they can spread between however many Influences you like. So a Rank 4 spirit could have an Influence at 4, 2 Influences at 2, 1 at 3 and 1 at 1, etc.<br /> <br /> Further Influence dots can be added to the spirit's Influence dot pool by giving up Numina slots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T14:18:39-07:00","id":483887,"title":"","content":"Prepering Dreadwolf as this particular NPC character Totem spirit. I have a problem with Bane of the being - Dreadwolf is symbolic spirit of crime commited to Mother Wolf on the end of Pangea, with his throat are slit all the time. So logical would be that the Bane could something like &quot;Claws and teeth of Uratha&quot; as the original symbol was that those things killed it. But it would make too easy for the PCs just too use their natural weapons as way to kill Dreadwolf.<br /> <br /> So as the Totem is Rank 4 being, maybe something like &quot;Claws of Traitor&quot; - in this way, the character needing to kill the Dreadwolf, must first betray his close ones - or even Dreadwolf himself. Should this not be better fitting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-20-2015, 03:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T23:24:20-07:00","id":486045,"title":"","content":"Ah yes... bans and banes. <br /> Spirits now have both a ban and a bane. <br /> <br /> Which is to say, they have a behaviour that they must obey, and a substance or condition which causes them to disintegrate/stop existing. <br /> <br /> In the above example, the claws and teeth of the Uratha could be a bane, but it seems to me that their claws and teeth would likely strengthen the spirit, since those are the things that birthed it. They aren't antithetical to the symbolism, they're a part of it. You could craft a behaviour that requires a werewolf to splash his hands/teeth with wolf blood before addressing him but that's almost more of an act of chimage. <br /> <br /> Perhaps more antithetical would be the tending of the elderly. Since Father wolf was killed by his children for failing to do his duty, possibly because he was poisoned at the time, someone continuing to care for their elderly parent/grandparent would be actively undoing the symbolism that birthed Dreadwolf. It might start off as an inconvenience, effectively allowing Dreadwolf to be repulsed by the sight of someone's ailing grandparent, to something much worse for dreadwolf (like he suffers aggravated simply by being in their presence).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5514-qcks","name":"Qcks","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T10:24:40-07:00","id":486492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Qcks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/476538-bale-hounds-how-powerfull-are-maeltinet?p=486045#post486045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps more antithetical would be the tending of the elderly. Since Father wolf was killed by his children for failing to do his duty, possibly because he was poisoned at the time, someone continuing to care for their elderly parent/grandparent would be actively undoing the symbolism that birthed Dreadwolf. It might start off as an inconvenience, effectively allowing Dreadwolf to be repulsed by the sight of someone's ailing grandparent, to something much worse for dreadwolf (like he suffers aggravated simply by being in their presence).</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case I'd make it vulnerable to the elderly themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}